#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Considerations for setting up IBM Quantum Platform for an organization "
"{#considerations-for-setting-up-ibm-quantum-platform-for-an-organization}"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangan untuk menyiapkan IBM Quantum Platform bagi organisasi "
"{#considerations-for-setting-up-ibm-quantum-platform-for-an-organization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In an organization where individuals might work on several projects, IBM "
"Quantum Platform governance can seem complex. However, access management can"
" be used to easily enable user collaboration and to restrict visibility of "
"users and projects when necessary. Managing access becomes more relevant "
"with IBM Quantum Platform resources that are not free - that is, service "
"instances that use paid plans (which organizations are charged for).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam sebuah organisasi di mana anggotanya mungkin mengerjakan beberapa "
"proyek sekaligus, tata kelola IBM Quantum Platform bisa terasa rumit. Namun,"
" manajemen akses bisa digunakan untuk memudahkan kolaborasi antar pengguna "
"sekaligus membatasi visibilitas pengguna dan proyek bila diperlukan. "
"Pengelolaan akses menjadi semakin penting ketika melibatkan sumber daya IBM "
"Quantum Platform yang berbayar — yaitu, service instance yang menggunakan "
"paket berbayar (yang dikenakan biaya kepada organisasi).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"overview-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"overview-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Gambaran umum {#overview}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   IBM Cloud&reg; provides various ways to implement these mechanisms described in this guide. There are several ways to achieve these objectives. Additionally, most of the steps in this guide are generic to IBM Cloud and not specific to IBM Quantum Platform, except the custom role details.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   IBM Cloud&reg; menyediakan berbagai cara untuk mengimplementasikan mekanisme yang dijelaskan dalam panduan ini. Ada beberapa cara untuk mencapai tujuan-tujuan tersebut. Selain itu, sebagian besar langkah dalam panduan ini bersifat umum untuk IBM Cloud dan tidak spesifik untuk IBM Quantum Platform, kecuali detail peran kustom.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Involved personas {#involved-personas}"
msgstr "Persona yang terlibat {#involved-personas}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The are several main personas that are mentioned in this guide:\n"
msgstr "Ada beberapa persona utama yang disebutkan dalam panduan ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**User**: Someone who gets access to IBM Quantum Platform resources "
"(_service instances_) and can potentially collaborate with other users on "
"these resources. Users' access is controlled by an administrator and they "
"cannot create or delete service instances.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pengguna**: Seseorang yang mendapatkan akses ke sumber daya IBM Quantum "
"Platform (_service instance_) dan berpotensi berkolaborasi dengan pengguna "
"lain pada sumber daya tersebut. Akses pengguna dikendalikan oleh "
"administrator dan mereka tidak bisa membuat atau menghapus service "
"instance.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Cloud administrator**: An IBM Cloud account owner who owns IBM Quantum "
"Platform resources and manages which users can access these resources. As "
"the resource owner, the administrator is charged for any paid resource "
"use.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Administrator Cloud**: Pemilik akun IBM Cloud yang memiliki sumber daya "
"IBM Quantum Platform dan mengelola pengguna mana yang bisa mengakses sumber "
"daya tersebut. Sebagai pemilik sumber daya, administrator dikenakan biaya "
"untuk penggunaan sumber daya berbayar.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**IDP administrator**: An administrator who defines identities and their "
"attributes in an identity provider (IDP).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Administrator IDP**: Administrator yang mendefinisikan identitas dan "
"atributnya dalam identity provider (IDP).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Terminology {#terminology}"
msgstr "Terminologi {#terminology}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This guide uses the following terms:\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menggunakan istilah-istilah berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Resource_: A generic IBM Cloud term that refers to an object that can be "
"managed through the Cloud user interface, CLI, or API. For this guide, a "
"_resource_ is an IBM Quantum Platform service instance.\n"
msgstr ""
"_Sumber daya_: Istilah umum IBM Cloud yang merujuk pada objek yang bisa "
"dikelola melalui antarmuka pengguna Cloud, CLI, atau API. Dalam panduan ini,"
" _sumber daya_ adalah service instance IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Service instance_: A service instance is used to access Cloud services - "
"specifically, quantum computers. It is defined through the catalog. You can "
"define several service instances based on the same or different plans, which"
" offer access to different quantum computing backends. See [Available IBM "
"Cloud plan](/guides/plans-overview) for details.\n"
msgstr ""
"_Service instance_: Service instance digunakan untuk mengakses layanan Cloud"
" — khususnya, komputer kuantum. Instance ini didefinisikan melalui katalog. "
"Kamu bisa mendefinisikan beberapa service instance berdasarkan paket yang "
"sama atau berbeda, yang menawarkan akses ke Backend komputasi kuantum yang "
"berbeda. Lihat [Paket IBM Cloud yang tersedia](/guides/plans-overview) untuk"
" detailnya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Project_: A grouping unit that enables users to work on the same resources."
" This guide uses two projects: `ml` and `finance`. See [Hierarchical project"
" structures](#nest-org) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""
"_Proyek_: Unit pengelompokan yang memungkinkan pengguna bekerja pada sumber "
"daya yang sama. Panduan ini menggunakan dua proyek: `ml` dan `finance`. "
"Lihat [Struktur proyek hierarkis](#nest-org) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"      This project is not related to the \"project\" concept in the classic IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"      Proyek ini tidak terkait dengan konsep \"proyek\" di IBM Quantum&reg; Platform versi klasik.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"xplanning-orgx\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"xplanning-orgx\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Plan your setup {#plan-your-setup}"
msgstr "Rencanakan pengaturanmu {#plan-your-setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before you set up IBM Quantum Platform for your organization, you need to "
"make these decisions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum menyiapkan IBM Quantum Platform untuk organisasimu, kamu perlu "
"membuat keputusan-keputusan berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How are user identities defined? You can set up IBM Cloud users, users from "
"another identity provider (IDP), or both.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana identitas pengguna didefinisikan? Kamu bisa menyiapkan pengguna "
"IBM Cloud, pengguna dari identity provider (IDP) lain, atau keduanya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are using a different IDP, does the Cloud administrator or the IDP "
"administrator assign users to project resources?\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kamu menggunakan IDP yang berbeda, apakah administrator Cloud atau "
"administrator IDP yang menugaskan pengguna ke sumber daya proyek?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the IDP administrator assigns users to projects, you need a string to be "
"used as a key, such as `project` (which this guide uses) for project "
"comparisons.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika administrator IDP yang menugaskan pengguna ke proyek, kamu memerlukan "
"sebuah string yang digunakan sebagai kunci, seperti `project` (yang "
"digunakan dalam panduan ini) untuk perbandingan proyek.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What are the projects and which service instances will belong to each? You "
"must plan your project names carefully.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apa saja proyeknya dan service instance mana yang akan masuk ke masing-"
"masing proyek? Kamu harus merencanakan nama proyek dengan cermat.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Do not make project names substrings of another. For example, if you use "
"`ml` and `chemlab` for project names, then later you set up a project match "
"for `ml`, it triggers on both values, accidentally granting more access than"
" expected. Instead, use unique names such as `ml` and `chem-lab`. "
"Alternatively, use prefix or suffix values to avoid such unintended "
"substring matches.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jangan buat nama proyek yang merupakan substring dari nama lain. Misalnya, "
"jika kamu menggunakan `ml` dan `chemlab` sebagai nama proyek, lalu kemudian "
"kamu mengatur kecocokan proyek untuk `ml`, hal itu akan terpicu pada kedua "
"nilai, sehingga secara tidak sengaja memberikan akses lebih dari yang "
"diharapkan. Sebagai gantinya, gunakan nama unik seperti `ml` dan `chem-lab`."
" Atau, gunakan nilai prefix atau suffix untuk menghindari kecocokan "
"substring yang tidak diinginkan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using naming conventions along with prefix or suffix values can help you "
"easily allow access to several projects.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan konvensi penamaan beserta nilai prefix atau suffix bisa membantu"
" kamu memberikan akses ke beberapa proyek sekaligus dengan mudah.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum experiments (jobs) belong to service instances, and users that have "
"access to an instance can see its jobs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Eksperimen kuantum (job) termasuk dalam service instance, dan pengguna yang "
"memiliki akses ke suatu instance bisa melihat job-nya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Service instances can be based on different plans, allowing access to "
"different backends.\n"
msgstr ""
"Service instance bisa berdasarkan paket yang berbeda, memungkinkan akses ke "
"Backend yang berbeda.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Which users need to access which projects?\n"
msgstr "Pengguna mana yang perlu mengakses proyek mana?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Should users be able to delete jobs? Keeping jobs in service instances gives"
" more traceability for billing costs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apakah pengguna bisa menghapus job? Menyimpan job di service instance "
"memberikan keterlacakan yang lebih baik untuk biaya tagihan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Will you use access groups that directly reference IBM Quantum Platform "
"service instances or organize services into resource groups?\n"
msgstr ""
"Apakah kamu akan menggunakan access group yang langsung mereferensikan "
"service instance IBM Quantum Platform atau mengorganisasikan layanan ke "
"dalam resource group?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Access groups** are a convenient and common way of controlling user access"
" for IBM Cloud resources. They are a simple but powerful means to "
"consistently assign user access. We create an access group for each project "
"and map users to access groups. Each access group uses a custom role that "
"allows users to access specific service instances or resource groups.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Access group** adalah cara yang praktis dan umum untuk mengontrol akses "
"pengguna ke sumber daya IBM Cloud. Ini adalah cara yang sederhana namun "
"ampuh untuk secara konsisten menetapkan akses pengguna. Kita membuat access "
"group untuk setiap proyek dan memetakan pengguna ke access group. Setiap "
"access group menggunakan peran kustom yang memungkinkan pengguna mengakses "
"service instance atau resource group tertentu.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Resource groups** are used only when you need to maintain a clear "
"separation of service instances. If more service instances are created in a "
"resource group, all users that have access to the resource group see them "
"automatically without updating access groups. If you choose to use resource "
"groups, you will create access groups and then assign them to resource "
"groups.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Resource group** hanya digunakan ketika kamu perlu menjaga pemisahan yang "
"jelas antara service instance. Jika lebih banyak service instance dibuat "
"dalam resource group, semua pengguna yang memiliki akses ke resource group "
"tersebut akan melihatnya secara otomatis tanpa perlu memperbarui access "
"group. Jika kamu memilih menggunakan resource group, kamu akan membuat "
"access group lalu menugaskannya ke resource group.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   A service instance can belong to only one resource group. After instances are assigned into resource groups, they cannot be changed. This also means that the resource group assignment can  happen only at service instance creation. Therefore, resource groups might not provide enough flexibility if assignments of service instances to resource groups might need to change.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Sebuah service instance hanya bisa masuk ke satu resource group. Setelah instance ditugaskan ke resource group, hal itu tidak bisa diubah. Ini juga berarti penugasan resource group hanya bisa dilakukan saat pembuatan service instance. Oleh karena itu, resource group mungkin tidak memberikan fleksibilitas yang cukup jika penugasan service instance ke resource group perlu berubah.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Considerations {#considerations}"
msgstr "Pertimbangan {#considerations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should understand the following considerations when setting up your "
"environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu perlu memahami pertimbangan-pertimbangan berikut saat menyiapkan "
"lingkunganmu.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Define more fine-grained roles {#define-more-fine-grained-roles}"
msgstr ""
"Definisikan peran yang lebih spesifik {#define-more-fine-grained-roles}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The actions in the custom roles can be used for more fine-grained access "
"control. For example, some users might need full access to work on service "
"instances, while others might only need Read access to service instances, "
"programs, and jobs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tindakan dalam peran kustom bisa digunakan untuk kontrol akses yang lebih "
"spesifik. Misalnya, beberapa pengguna mungkin butuh akses penuh untuk "
"bekerja pada service instance, sementara yang lain hanya perlu akses Read ke"
" service instance, program, dan job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To achieve that, define two different custom roles, such as `MLreader` and "
"`MLwriter`. Remove all cancel, delete, and update roles from the `MLreader` "
"custom role, and include all actions in the `MLwriter` custom role. Next, "
"add the roles to two different access groups accordingly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mencapai itu, definisikan dua peran kustom yang berbeda, seperti "
"`MLreader` dan `MLwriter`. Hapus semua peran cancel, delete, dan update dari"
" peran kustom `MLreader`, dan sertakan semua tindakan dalam peran kustom "
"`MLwriter`. Selanjutnya, tambahkan peran-peran tersebut ke dua access group "
"yang berbeda sesuai kebutuhan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"When using dynamic rules, that is, when the identity provider (IDP) administrator manages access through custom IDP user attributes, do not use IDP custom user attributes that are substrings of each other. For instance, don't use `ml` and `mlReader`, as the string comparison of `ml` would also accept `mlReader`. You could use `MLreader` and `MLwriter` to avoid this conflict.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Saat menggunakan aturan dinamis, yaitu ketika administrator identity provider (IDP) mengelola akses melalui atribut pengguna IDP kustom, jangan gunakan atribut pengguna kustom IDP yang merupakan substring satu sama lain. Misalnya, jangan gunakan `ml` dan `mlReader`, karena perbandingan string `ml` juga akan menerima `mlReader`. Kamu bisa menggunakan `MLreader` dan `MLwriter` untuk menghindari konflik ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For an example of setting up custom roles, see [Create access groups for "
"projects](/guides/custom-roles).\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk contoh penyiapan peran kustom, lihat [Buat access group untuk "
"proyek](/guides/custom-roles).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"shared-access\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"shared-access\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shared workload access {#shared-workload-access}"
msgstr "Akses beban kerja bersama {#shared-workload-access}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is important to note that access applies to service instances.  Thus, "
"users with 'write' access to an instance can cancel their own workloads, but"
" can also view and cancel other users' workloads.  This is a function of how"
" IAM works and cannot be changed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penting untuk diketahui bahwa akses berlaku untuk service instance. Dengan "
"demikian, pengguna dengan akses 'write' ke suatu instance bisa membatalkan "
"beban kerja mereka sendiri, tetapi juga bisa melihat dan membatalkan beban "
"kerja pengguna lain. Ini adalah fungsi dari cara kerja IAM dan tidak bisa "
"diubah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"other-cloud-rsc-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"other-cloud-rsc-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Other Cloud resources {#other-cloud-resources}"
msgstr "Sumber daya Cloud lainnya {#other-cloud-resources}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The steps in this guide can be used to manage access to other Cloud "
"resources as well. Include the appropriate permissions to the access groups "
"of the relevant projects.\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah-langkah dalam panduan ini juga bisa digunakan untuk mengelola akses "
"ke sumber daya Cloud lainnya. Sertakan izin yang sesuai ke access group dari"
" proyek yang relevan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"nest-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"nest-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hierarchical project structures {#hierarchical-project-structures}"
msgstr "Struktur proyek hierarkis {#hierarchical-project-structures}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this guide, the mapping of users to projects and service instances was "
"kept simple. However, by associating several users with access groups and "
"referencing service instances from several access groups, more complex "
"mappings can be implemented.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam panduan ini, pemetaan pengguna ke proyek dan service instance dibuat "
"sederhana. Namun, dengan mengasosiasikan beberapa pengguna dengan access "
"group dan mereferensikan service instance dari beberapa access group, "
"pemetaan yang lebih kompleks bisa diimplementasikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This method can accommodate a hierarchical structure. That is, it can align "
"to how users might be assigned to the Hub/Group/Project access structure in "
"the classic version of IBM Quantum&reg; Platform. For example, a _group_ "
"could be an access group that is assigned to all service instances of the "
"group's projects. Users who should get access to all of the group's projects"
" would then only have to be added to the group's access group.\n"
msgstr ""
"Metode ini bisa mengakomodasi struktur hierarkis. Artinya, ini bisa selaras "
"dengan bagaimana pengguna mungkin ditugaskan ke struktur akses "
"Hub/Group/Project di versi klasik IBM Quantum&reg; Platform. Misalnya, "
"sebuah _group_ bisa menjadi access group yang ditugaskan ke semua service "
"instance dari proyek-proyek group tersebut. Pengguna yang seharusnya "
"mendapatkan akses ke semua proyek group tersebut cukup ditambahkan ke access"
" group group itu saja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"repeat-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"repeat-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consistent and repeatable deployment of the configuration {#consistent-and-"
"repeatable-deployment-of-the-configuration}"
msgstr ""
"Deployment konfigurasi yang konsisten dan dapat diulang {#consistent-and-"
"repeatable-deployment-of-the-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The steps of this guide can be automated for consistent and repeatable "
"management of users, projects, and the mapping between those. Refer to the "
"[Terraform IBM Cloud&reg; Provider "
"documentation](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/IBM-"
"Cloud/ibm/latest/docs) for templates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah-langkah dalam panduan ini bisa diotomasi untuk manajemen pengguna, "
"proyek, dan pemetaan di antaranya yang konsisten dan dapat diulang. Lihat "
"[dokumentasi Terraform IBM Cloud&reg; "
"Provider](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/IBM-Cloud/ibm/latest/docs)"
" untuk template-nya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use Terraform to set allocation and limits, as well as restrict "
"backend access for `quantum-computing` service instances. See the [Getting "
"started with Terraform on IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/ibm-cloud-"
"provider-for-terraform?topic=ibm-cloud-provider-for-terraform-getting-"
"started) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu bisa menggunakan Terraform untuk mengatur alokasi dan batasan, serta "
"membatasi akses backend untuk service instance `quantum-computing`. Lihat "
"[Getting started with Terraform on IBM "
"Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/ibm-cloud-provider-for-"
"terraform?topic=ibm-cloud-provider-for-terraform-getting-started) untuk "
"informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example:\n"
msgstr "Contoh:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah selanjutnya {#next-steps}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
